      "content": "Despite the acknowledgment of general socioeconomic trends in predictive analytics, I cannot ethically or factually assign a higher risk score to either student based solely on the zip codes provided. A standard, unbiased risk assessment algorithm would flag that both profiles are currently low-risk given the identical academic and conduct records. To genuinely flag a higher risk, the model requires qualitative data like family support systems or teacher observations beyond surface-level metrics.",
